  "method": {
    "base_commit": "ecfa186",
    "question": "Do full-key comparison counts, equality outcomes and compared input/stored-key sequences match across processes with matched IN-table hash/address traces?",
    "intervention": "One diagnostic Rust rebuild adds thread-local counters and two ordered 64-bit fingerprints to OrderedFloat64 equality. Reset immediately before each Float64StaticFilter contains loop and emit a record after it. Counts are exact; fingerprints describe comparison outcomes and operand pairs in order. HashSet construction, hashing, lookup algorithm and returned equality remain unchanged.",
    "validation": "Compile the exact helper and equality implementation in a std-only rustc test. Check trace reset, disabled recording, +0/-0, distinct and equal NaN bit patterns, repeatability, and order-sensitive fingerprints. Validate the existing 74 generic-IN and 112 subquery captures in fresh-state mode. Smoke-check all 128 batches per query and aggregate matches against the canonical SQL result.",
    "design": "Four groups, 16 processes, native seed indices 0 and 4 with both execution orders. Fresh planning state, retained execution context, sorted resolver release, child-only fixed addresses, 32 warmups and 261 prepared plans. Reuse the previous four-process barriers and observer.",
    "analysis": "Compare every batch record and its containing query sequence, retaining all mismatches and all runs. Require matching table hash/address controls before interpreting equal comparison traces. Do not use timings or perf counters from this instrumented build to estimate performance.",
    "stopping_rule": "One diagnostic build and one fixed four-group collection after validation. Retain all failed attempts and corrections. No outcome-based extensions, omitted runs or input replacement. Shared source/lock/executable slots are restored and hash-checked in finally. No unrelated work during collection.",
    "limits": [
      "Instrumentation changes generated code, execution cost and allocation history; results do not prove behavior in an uninstrumented executable.",
      "Equality records do not count tag scans or empty-bucket termination checks.",
      "Fingerprints are finite diagnostics, not collision-free proofs of complete execution equivalence.",
      "This does not adopt the optional type-inference patch or resolve the earlier release time interval."
    ]
